# The demo needs NONE of this: without a .env.local file the app runs on demo
# data kept in your browser.
#
# To use Supabase: copy this file to `.env.local` (same folder) and fill in the
# values. `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit real values, and never share
# keys.
#
# Only variables starting with VITE_ are exposed to the browser. That is safe for
# everything below: these values are public by design, and data is protected by
# Row Level Security and server functions, not by hiding them.
#
# NEVER put the Supabase secret key (sb_secret_... or the legacy service_role key)
# in this file. It belongs only in Edge Function secrets.

# Where data comes from: `mock` (demo data in this browser, the default) or
# `supabase`.
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE=mock

# Set to `client` only for a build meant for real clients. Such a build refuses
# to start (and to build) on demo data.
# VITE_RELEASE=client

# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API (use the tallybox-dev project locally)
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys > Publishable key (sb_publishable_...)
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Cloudflare dashboard > Turnstile > site key (public).
# For local testing, Cloudflare's always-pass test site key is 1x00000000000000000000AA
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Optional. Domain used to build staff sign-in addresses. Leave unset for the
# default (tallybox.invalid). Must match STAFF_EMAIL_DOMAIN in the Edge Functions.
# VITE_STAFF_EMAIL_DOMAIN=
